From: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] extract-cert: Skip the PKCS#11 ENGINE path when OpenSSL lacks
 ENGINE

OpenSSL 4 removed the ENGINE implementation. It still installs
<openssl/engine.h>, so extract-cert.c compiles, but every ENGINE_* symbol
is gone from libcrypto and the host tool fails to link:

  undefined reference to `ENGINE_load_builtin_engines'
  undefined reference to `ENGINE_by_id'

which breaks do_compile for any kernel old enough to predate the upstream
migration (v6.x, "sign-file,extract-cert: use pkcs11 provider for OPENSSL
MAJOR >= 3").

ENGINE is used only to read a certificate from a pkcs11: URI. Guard that
branch with OpenSSL's own OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE, which the OpenSSL 4 headers
define, so a file-based CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_KEY -- what this BSP uses -- is
unaffected. A pkcs11: source now fails with a clear diagnostic instead of
not linking at all.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific]

Backporting the upstream provider-based rewrite would pull in its
supporting header refactor; this keeps the change local to the ENGINE use
that no longer links.

Signed-off-by: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
---
 scripts/extract-cert.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scripts/extract-cert.c b/scripts/extract-cert.c
--- a/scripts/extract-cert.c
+++ b/scripts/extract-cert.c
@@ -21,7 +21,9 @@
 #include <openssl/bio.h>
 #include <openssl/pem.h>
 #include <openssl/err.h>
+#ifndef OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE
 #include <openssl/engine.h>
+#endif
 
 #define PKEY_ID_PKCS7 2
 
@@ -112,6 +114,7 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
 		fclose(f);
 		exit(0);
 	} else if (!strncmp(cert_src, "pkcs11:", 7)) {
+#ifndef OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE
 		ENGINE *e;
 		struct {
 			const char *cert_id;
@@ -133,6 +136,11 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
 		ENGINE_ctrl_cmd(e, "LOAD_CERT_CTRL", 0, &parms, NULL, 1);
 		ERR(!parms.cert, "Get X.509 from PKCS#11");
 		write_cert(parms.cert);
+#else
+		fprintf(stderr,
+			"extract-cert: this OpenSSL build has no ENGINE support; pkcs11: sources are unavailable\n");
+		exit(1);
+#endif
 	} else {
 		BIO *b;
 		X509 *x509;
